=== M109 AC-01 (S1) — ac_verify::execute and pipe_drain_thread distinguish io::ErrorKind ===

C-1 fix landed in crates/mp/src/ac_verify.rs:

  fn execute(...) {
      // M109 (C-1): retry on EINTR (which is normal on a signal-
      // interrupted syscall), surface any other try_wait error with
      // its ErrorKind so the orchestrator / VerifyReport can diagnose
      // ECHILD (already reaped by a parent), ESRCH (no such process),
      // EPERM, etc. distinctly from the per-AC timeout.
      let try_wait_done = match child.try_wait() {
          Ok(Some(status)) => break status,
          Ok(None) => false,
          Err(e) if e.kind() == std::io::ErrorKind::Interrupted => false,
          Err(e) => {
              return Err(format!(
                  "try_wait failed: kind={:?} error={}",
                  e.kind(),
                  e
              ));
          }
      };
      if !try_wait_done && start.elapsed() >= timeout {
          ...
      }
      if !try_wait_done {
          thread::sleep(Duration::from_millis(50));
      }
  }

  fn pipe_drain_thread<R>(...) {
      loop {
          match pipe.read(&mut chunk) {
              Ok(0) => break, // EOF
              Ok(n) => { ... }
              Err(e) if e.kind() == std::io::ErrorKind::Interrupted => continue,
              Err(e) => {
                  let note = format!("<drain error: {e}>");
                  buf.lock().extend_from_slice(note.as_bytes());
                  break;
              }
          }
      }
  }

Verification:
  $ grep -qE 'ErrorKind::Interrupted' crates/mp/src/ac_verify.rs
  (matches; confirmed)

  $ cargo test -p mp --lib ac_verify::tests::pipe_drain_thread
  running 5 tests
  test pipe_drain_thread_handles_eof_immediately ... ok
  test pipe_drain_thread_drains_small_input ... ok
  test pipe_drain_thread_records_error_kind_on_non_eintr ... ok   [NEW M109]
  test pipe_drain_thread_retries_on_interrupted_error ... ok        [NEW M109]
  test pipe_drain_thread_drains_large_input ... ok
  test result: ok. 5 passed; 0 failed

The two new unit tests exercise:
  (1) Reading returns Err(Other) -> drain thread appends
      `<drain error: synthetic drain error>` sentinel and breaks.
      Pre-C-1, the loop broke silently with no sentinel.
  (2) Reading returns Err(Interrupted) -> drain thread retries.
      Pre-C-1, the loop broke silently on EINTR.

Both unit-test behaviors are now fixed and pinned by regression.

